  "description": "A global statistics library, this module offers a comprehensive suite of functions \n      for calculating mathematical statistics on real-valued numerical data. Designed for \n      precision and ease, FTI.Statistics empowers users to delve into robust statistical \n      analysis with unparalleled efficiency.\n\n      *Unless explicitly noted, these functions support `int`, `float`, `Decimal`, and `Fraction`. \n      Behavior with other types (whether in the numeric tower or not) is currently unsupported. \n      Collections with a mix of types are also undefined and implementation-dependent. \n      If your input data consists of mixed types, you may be able to use `map()` to ensure a \n      consistent result, for example: `map(float, input_data).*",
  "id": "FTI.Statistics",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2025-07-02T07:14:04.833Z",
